# JSON-LD page schemas

## Placement

- Define **`{pageName}PageSchema()`** on the page itself (e.g. `homePageSchema`, `termsPageSchema`, `articlePageSchema`).
- Do **not** put page schemas in `src/lib/schema.ts`.
- `lib/schema.ts` only: `jsonLdScript`, `breadcrumbSchema`, `organizationSchema`, shared ids/helpers.

## Shape

```ts
function cookiePolicyPageSchema() {
  const pageUrl = absoluteUrl(paths.cookiePolicy);
  return {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "WebPage",
        "@id": `${pageUrl}#webpage`,
        url: pageUrl,
        name: title,
        description,
        inLanguage: site.locale,
      },
      breadcrumbSchema([
        { name: "Home", path: paths.home },
        { name: title, path: paths.cookiePolicy },
      ]),
    ],
  };
}
```

Render with `dangerouslySetInnerHTML={jsonLdScript(cookiePolicyPageSchema())}`.

## Home / sitewide

- Home graph typically includes Organization + WebSite (+ optional `SearchAction` when the product has search) + WebPage.
- Detail/list schemas (Article, Product, JobPosting, etc.) live on that page — not in `lib/`.
